{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented as change https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1680 (commit 6cb803c918, stacked on 1673).\n\nPREMISE VERIFIED. force_close_reason was declared at txn.py:198 and occurred exactly once in the file — accepted and never read — while transition_close passed the operator's --force=<reason> into it. Confirmed real.\n\nCHANGE. Written onto the *->closed STATUS event present-only, folded into reduced state, mirroring close_class at every step: same write guard, same winner-only fold (so a losing concurrent close cannot overwrite the winner's reason), same ticket_state.schema.json declaration. Renamed _fold_close_class -> _fold_close_metadata since it now folds two fields on that edge; only 3 references, all in one file.\n\nEVIDENCE. 4 new tests, 15 passing in tests/unit/test_transition_close.py. Wider -k 'transition or close or reduc or txn or state or schema': 874 passed, 3 skipped. make lint (incl. complexity baseline) and make typecheck (512 files) clean. Regenerated src/rebar/types.py via python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types after the schema edit — that file is GENERATED, and hand-editing it is what caused damselfly's first CI failure.\n\nTWO TEST-CONSTRUCTION FINDINGS worth recording, because both would have made a green test that proved nothing:\n\n1. Raw STATUS event files do not survive a close. _compact_on_close absorbs them into a SNAPSHOT, so a post-close glob finds zero *-STATUS.json. The two tests asserting on the raw event now disable compaction explicitly (it is orthogonal to what they assert); the reduced-state test needs no such help and reads through the snapshot, which is the better evidence for AC2 anyway.\n\n2. My first helper guessed the tracker path (repo/.tickets-tracker/<id>). It now resolves through rebar's own config.tracker_dir and asserts the event list is non-empty before indexing, so a moved layout FAILS loudly instead of silently passing an empty-list assertion.\n\nAC4 is pinned structurally rather than behaviourally: test_transition_core_does_not_accept_a_parameter_it_discards inspects transition_core's source and asserts every close-metadata parameter it declares is actually read in the body. That is the defect class itself — a parameter accepted and dropped — so it guards close_class and force_close_reason against rotting into no-ops the same way."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786567590928999001,"uuid":"63c5c649-0945-4adb-ae91-d8e77103e455"}